To get around this, one can set autoquiver in one's NH options file.
Appropriate ammunition will be automatically selected for you.  I
don't know the semantics because I don't use autoquiver, so YMMV.

One can use (t)hrow even when one has quivered ammunition readied.
For example, if I have a small stack of highly enchanted "emergency
use only" arrows and a large stack of (disposable) +0 arrows.  I'll
quiver the +0 stuff and throw the enchanted stuff when I want to use
it instead.

